  "title": "The One-Trip Grocery Pride",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "everyday microdramas",
  "premise": "A shopper insists on carrying every empty prop bag in one trip, turning into a wobbling tower of handles. They set everything down, make two easy trips, and discover that the dramatic ONE TRIP badge can be folded into a useful shelf label reading TWO IS FINE.",
  "hook": "One trip. Seventeen handles. A questionable victory.",
  "visible_action": "Bag handles collect along arms; tower sways; bags are set down; two small loads cross the frame; badge folds into a label.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "A self-imposed rule can be dropped when it makes the task worse.",
  "gate": "Use visibly lightweight empty bags; no lifting limits, injury claims, or unsafe-load demonstration.",
